title The card refreshed, so the loop wakes into a tree it agrees with
prompt refresh the card
think Left a cairn first, because the rule asks for one before any debride that rewrites a living card and this shed nineteen rows. The walk-back names what waits there honestly: the per-fold reasoning, which is the Caravan arc's real teaching and is not summarised well by a count.
think Refreshed for a reader who is not a person. The outer loop takes the door the card names, so a stale live edge is not untidy -- it is an instruction. The card's edge was fold AI from eight hours earlier, and the loop's first act would very likely have been fold AJ, a mark the mark law seated today explicitly retires.
think Wrote three new rows rather than one. The edge says what happened; the standing equipment says what the tree now HAS, since a loop that does not know it owns seventeen guards will not run them; and the next doors say what to do, written in the vocabulary the day seated.
think Put the run-them-first habit into the equipment row in the words the day earned: a guard earns confidence by being run, not by being written. Two of the newest were red the first time they were asked, which is the evidence rather than the sentiment.
think Named the Caravan work as continuing rather than finished, and named it as LIFT. The arc is real and unfinished; retiring the ascending mark does not retire the work, and a card that said only what was forbidden would leave the loop with nothing to do.
obs The condensation paid part of a debt the card names in its own INNER LOOP -- 58,608 bytes down to 42,808, nineteen rows to four. The remaining debt is smaller and still real.
obs Checked the e123 living-pin guard as well as the ASCII one, since that guard keys on the card's own headers and pins and has red on exactly this kind of edit before (REDS %87). Green.
loom card=refreshed bytes_before=58608 after=42808 rows_before=19 after=4 cairn=5f09ec4273
loom guards=17 green=17 e123_living_pin=green census_lost=192 ceiling=192
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge, the standing equipment, the next doors, and the arc condensed
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back to nineteen rows and the reasoning inside them
recommend check-in (Keaton) the card agrees with the tree now and the loop can restart into it. Worth one deliberate choice before it does: the next-doors row names the Caravan lift work, the two Season G doors, and two held items, and whichever the loop opens first it will open unattended -- so picking that first door by hand, or watching one lap, is the conservative move after a day that seated this much law.
